{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe scheduled **Verify Authorship Identity** workflow (`.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`, job `verify-identity (authenticated-authorship gate)`) fails at the step **\"Fail closed if the blobless checkout pack exceeds its limit\"**. The guard compares `git count-objects -v` `size-pack:` against `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` (verify-identity.yml:47, value `102400` KiB = 100 MiB) and fails closed when exceeded.\n\nDecisive log (run 33253701193, sha `5fb693345b0c`):\n```\nREBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 102400\n##[error]checkout pack is 492830 KiB; limit is 102400 KiB\n##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\n```\nSo the checkout pack is **492830 KiB ≈ 481 MiB**, ~4.8× the 100 MiB limit.\n\n## This is a regression, not a chronic config\n\n`Verify Authorship Identity` history (schedule, ~4×/day) shows a clean green→red boundary:\n- last success: `2026-08-23T01:20:35Z`\n- first failure: `2026-08-23T07:07:44Z`\n- red on **every** run since (12+ consecutive at time of filing, through 2026-08-29T12:55).\n\nSo the pack crossed the 100 MiB threshold around 2026-08-23 and has kept growing. Failing runs in window: 33239620291, 33253701193 (both sha `5fb693345b0c`), plus the same failure every prior scheduled run back to 2026-08-23.\n\n## Root cause hypothesis\n\nRepo/tickets-branch object growth pushed the blobless checkout pack past the CI limit. This correlates with tickets-store growth — see closed P1 bug `absurd-zoometric-bobwhite` (f9ee-5ad5-4a78-4147, \"tickets branch/store exceeds 1 GiB after history reclaim\"). The reclaim there targeted a fresh clone ≤150 MB, but the CI gate's blobless checkout is now 481 MiB, so either growth resumed post-reclaim or the 100 MiB limit no longer reflects the store's steady-state size. It also plausibly correlates with the gerrit data-disk-high alarm / AWS data-disk sweep (repo growth on the box).\n\n## What needs deciding\n\n1. Is 481 MiB expected steady-state (limit too low → raise `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` deliberately), or is this unbounded growth that needs another reclaim/gc / packing-strategy fix?\n2. Quantify current pack composition (blob vs tree vs history, tickets branch vs main) to attribute the growth — mirror the methodology used in f9ee.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Current `size-pack` for the exact CI checkout reproduced and attributed by object type / ref.\n- [x] Root cause of the 08-23 crossing identified (growth event vs limit-too-low).\n- [x] Either the limit is intentionally re-set with justification, or the growth is reclaimed so the gate is green, with evidence of a passing `Verify Authorship Identity` run.\n\n## Evidence\n- Failing run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33253701193 (sha `5fb693345b0c`)\n- Earlier same failure: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33239620291\n- Limit source: `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml:47` (`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 102400`); guard at lines 62-63.\n\n**AC completion evidence (see resolution comment 2026-08-29):** AC1/AC2 met by the Stage-1 dossier + Phase-1-exit RCA comments (481 MiB pack, ~90% tree objects; proven 08-23 organic growth step-change). AC3 met via the \"limit intentionally re-set with justification\" arm: budget raised 100→550 MiB by commit d0bcd6202789 (ticket a8ba, closed), restore tracked by 0894; passing run = Verify Authorship Identity scheduled run 33285210617 (sha 454f875e, 2026-08-30T01:14Z, success). Evidence is CI/history/cross-ticket (outside the code snapshot)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788064040267921677,"uuid":"3a4d4e87-8c31-4f45-b311-4188ec17fe05"}